      <div class="proc-doc__title">Regarding Richard Dent, District Attorney</div>
      <div class="proc-doc__issued">Issued in New York City on the 14th of October, 1962.</div>
      <p class="proc-doc__summary">The Office has determined that the District Attorney's office acted past what the law gives it during the tenure of Richard Dent. By section 1 of the Determination, the Department of Culture is charged with securing and examining the records of that office for the period of his tenure, and with reporting what is produced, what is outstanding and what is missing to the Public Advocate. Surrendered copies pass to the Office for Information, Records, and Patents.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size:.95rem">The Determination is the Office's standing lesson: an office that acts beyond its mandate is not forgiven twice.</p>
